        r.set("equation_accuracy",V::makeStr("native.op equation with analytic:{kind:polynomial,x:[ascending coefficients],y:[],z:[]} and t0/t1 creates exact degree<=25 polynomial Bezier geometry. Analytic circle/ellipse use center,normal,x_axis,radius or major/minor and t0/t1 radians. Arbitrary x(t),y(t),z(t) expressions use native:{op:equation,x,y,z,t0,t1,samples:2..512 (required),tolerance?:mm}, for example a conical spring path with samples:160 over t1:'8*pi'; they use adaptive interpolation and tolerance with seven native checkpoints per interval; capacity failures reject. This is observed error evidence, with no general bound between samples. Keep authored formulas; inspect exact_analytic_kind or equation_accuracy_evidence rather than treating display samples as formula proof."));
        r.set("varying_sweep",V::makeStr("Sweep native.sections:[{section:sketch,fraction:0..1,roll?:degrees,x_axis?:[x,y,z]}] accepts 2..32 strictly ordered sections including0 and1, instead of native.section. Fraction is path arc length; local XY profiles move to dynamic exact-tangent frames, with transported orientation and optional guide/roll. Named sketch/curve native.path remains associative. Native surface_spline takes UV controls (2..26), optional positive weights, one input face or semantic face; this retains an exact curve on that surface. Unsupported/ambiguous frames reject atomically."));
